   1:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** /* Roadmap:
   2:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 1) implement linkwitz riley filter
   3:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 2) create parameters to control where splits happen 
   4:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 3) prove that splitting into 3 bands doesn't produce artifacts
   5:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 4) create audio parameters for the 3 compressor bands
   6:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 5) add 2 remaning compressors
   7:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 6) ability to mute solo bypass individual compressors
   8:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 7) add input and output gain to offset changes in output level
   9:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 8) delete these comments
  10:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** */
  11:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  12:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** /*  How to derive butterworth filter coefficients: from the s domain transfer function:
  13:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** https://stackoverflow.com/questions/20924868/calculate-coefficients-of-2nd-order-butterworth-low-pa
  14:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  15:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** starting with the transferfuction for the butterworth filter
  16:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** G(s) = wc^2 / (s^2 + s*sqrt(2)*wc + wc^2)
  17:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  18:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** where "wc" is the cutoff frequency, apply the biliniar z-transform, i.e. substitute s = 2/T*(1-z^-1
  19:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** where T is the sampling period
  20:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  21:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** thus our transfer function in z domain is:
  22:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** g(z) = wc^2 / ((2/T*(1-z^-1)/(1+z^-1))^2 + (2/T*(1-z^-1)/(1+z^-1))*sqrt(2)*wc + wc^2)
  23:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  24:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** the cutoff frequency needs to be pre-warmped to compensate for the non-lienar relation between anal
  25:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  26:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** wc = 2/T * tan(wd*T/2)
  27:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** where "wd" is the "desired" cutoff frequency in [rads/s]
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Marcus\AppData\Local\Temp\ccq1dZ2b.s 			page 24


  28:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  29:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** let C = tan(wd*T/2), for convenience, so taht wc = 2/T*C
  30:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  31:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** substituting this into the equation, the 2/T factor drops out:
  32:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  33:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** G(z) = C^2 / ((1-z^-1)/(1+z^-1))^2 + (1-z^-1)/(1+z^-1)*sqrt(2)*C + C^2)
  34:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  35:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** multiply the numerator and denominator by (1+z^-1)^2 and expand, which yields:
  36:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  37:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** G(z) = C^2*(1 + 2*z^-1 + z^-2) / (1 + sqrt(2)*C + C^2 + 2*(C^2-1)*z^-1 + (1-sqrt(2)*C+C^2)*z^-2')
  38:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  39:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** Now, divide both numerator and denominator by the constant term from the denominator. For convenien
  40:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  41:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** G(z) = C^2/D*(1 + 2*z^-1 + z^-2) / (1 + 2*(C^2-1)/D*z^-1 + (1-sqrt(2)*C+C^2)/D*z^-2')
  42:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  43:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** This form is equivalent to the one we are looking for:
  44:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  45:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** G(z) = (b0 + b1*z^-1 + b2*z^-1) / (1 + a1*z^-1 +a2*z^-2)
  46:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  47:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** So we get the coefficients by equating them:
  48:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  49:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** a0 = 1
  50:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  51:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** a1 = 2*(C^2-1)/D
  52:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  53:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** a2 = (1-sqrt(2)*C+C^2)/D
  54:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  55:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** b0 = C^2/D
  56:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  57:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** b1 = 2*b0
  58:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  59:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** b2 = b0
  60:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  61:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** where, again, D = 1 + sqrt(2)*C + C^2, C = tan(wd*T/2), wd is the desired cutoff frequency [rad/s],
  62:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  63:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  64:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  65:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** FYI If you need a high pass filter coefs, all you have to do is use the same code:
  66:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  67:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** const double ita =1.0/ tan(M_PI*ff);
  68:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** const double q=sqrt(2.0);
  69:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** b0 = 1.0 / (1.0 + q*ita + ita*ita);
  70:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** b1= 2*b0;
  71:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** b2= b0;
  72:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** a1 = 2.0 * (ita*ita - 1.0) * b0;
  73:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** a2 = -(1.0 - q*ita + ita*ita) * b0;
  74:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  75:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** but then after multiply all your b terms by ita^2 and negate b1
  76:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  77:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** b0 = b0*ita*ita;
  78:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** b1 = -b1*ita*ita;
  79:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** b2 = b2*ita*ita;
  80:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  81:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** now you have a 2nd order high pass filter
  82:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
  83:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** */
  84:MultibandCompressor.cpp **** 
